				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Grove): Reformat transport send and metrics methods for readability\n\nAdjust whitespace in TransportAdapter to improve code clarity. The send_notification method's transport call is split across multiple lines for consistent formatting with surrounding code. The metrics method gains blank lines around the notifications_sent counter read to visually separate the metric construction from the return statement.\n\nNo functional changes — purely formatting improvements in the Grove transport layer.",
			"SHA": "1826c013c4c30e5940a4dd4a7527b9527d42ac85"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T14:30:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				80,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Grove): Track fire-and-forget notification count in transport metrics\n\nAdd an atomic counter to TransportAdapter to track notifications sent via send_notification. The counter increments on successful fire-and-forget sends and is exposed through the metrics() method, replacing the previous hardcoded zero value.\n\n- Add notifications_sent: Arc<AtomicU64> field to TransportAdapter\n- Initialize counter in new() and new_with_config() constructors\n- Update translate_metrics to accept notifications_sent parameter\n- Increment counter in send_notification on successful send\n- Return actual count from metrics() instead of empty TransportMetrics\n\nThis provides observability for one-way notification traffic over the Grove transport, completing the metrics picture alongside request/response tracking.",
			"SHA": "181d0f7d1d462d00dce06b857e364d7bbc742357"
		}
	],
